{
	"name": "Jack Chains",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/tools/fasteners/chain-steel-grey.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Strapped onto the sleeves of a jacket or a gambeson, jack chains consist of a series of metal plates connected by chain links to maintain mobility. They generally consist of a large shoulder plate, a large elbow plate, and a forearm plate. While this is the traditional structure of jack chains as a historical, and very well received, armor option, you can also apply this concept to other forms of piecemeal armor. Such as characters wearing a few pieces of heavy bones strapped to their limbs, or the sleeves of plate armor without the breastplate in place, to shift up your narrative variety.</p><p>While wearing light or medium armor, you can attach jack chains to gain a +1 bonus to AC. However you also gain disadvantage on stealth checks due to the rattle of the chains.</p>",
